{"parentUuid":"927da3ff-f74e-47c9-aa89-b06545043a4f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WwtYM8hXENzqgtNBYjJtSS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E97mX7pvoqgR3ZaR9B5kLs","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"Ray\" \"spot instances\" cost optimization batch jobs cloud 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7424,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":487,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7424},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":487,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7424,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxkFNzNd727Aoys9SDQ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c060cb3f-d873-4241-acb0-a4d6efc736bc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:33.390Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"44245dc2-5b5d-4fed-a141-14271db36053","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019TbaFKNwqkRABwjaRDSmzQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ray Tune hyperparameter tuning CP-SAT solver parameters search 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Ray Tune: Hyperparameter Tuning — Ray 2.55.1 - Ray Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/tune/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hyperparameter tuning using Ray Tune — PyTorch Tutorials 2.11.0+cu130 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.pytorch.org/tutorials/beginner/hyperparameter_tuning_tutorial.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-autotune: WIP: Tune the hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver for specific models · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune\"},{\"title\":\"Hyperparameter Search with Transformers and Ray Tune\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/ray-tune\"},{\"title\":\"Ray Tune: Hyperparameter Tuning — Ray 2.55.1\",\"url\":\"https://www.ray.io/ray-tune\"},{\"title\":\"Ray Tune: Hyperparameter Tuning — Ray 3.0.0.dev0\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/master/tune/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Running Tune experiments with Optuna — Ray 2.55.1\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/tune/examples/optuna_example.html\"},{\"title\":\"Ray Tune: Hyperparameter Tuning — Ray 2.50.1\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/tune/\"},{\"title\":\"Hyperparameter Tuning with Ray Tune — Ray 2.55.1\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/train/user-guides/hyperparameter-optimization.html\"},{\"title\":\"Cutting edge hyperparameter tuning with Ray Tune | by Richard Liaw | riselab | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/riselab/cutting-edge-hyperparameter-tuning-with-ray-tune-be6c0447afdf\"}]\n\n## Search Results Summary\n\nI found relevant information about Ray Tune hyperparameter tuning and CP-SAT solver parameter search. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n### Ray Tune Overview\nTune is a Python library for experiment execution and hyperparameter tuning at any scale. Tune integrates with a wide range of additional hyperparameter optimization tools, including Ax, BayesOpt, BOHB, Nevergrad, and Optuna.\n\n### CP-SAT Parameter Tuning\nThe search revealed a specialized project called **cpsat-autotune** that focuses specifically on tuning Google's OR-Tools CP-SAT solver. By tuning the solver's hyperparameters to optimize performance on typical instances, cpsat-autotune can reduce the average time per iteration, which is particularly valuable in ALNS, where a large number of solver calls are made.\n\n### CP-SAT Tuning Methods\nThe cpsat-autotune CLI provides three main commands: time, quality, and gap, with the time command tuning CP-SAT hyperparameters to minimize the time required to find an optimal solution.\n\n### Key Parameters for CP-SAT Tuning\nThe tuning process uses parameters like n_samples_for_trial (the number of samples taken in each trial), n_samples_for_verification (the number of samples used to verify parameters), and n_trials (the number of trials to run).\n\nThe search results show that while Ray Tune is the primary hyperparameter optimization framework, CP-SAT solver parameter tuning has its own specialized tools and methodologies through the cpsat-autotune project.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"52b64b1a-da7c-48b5-b4c9-442fda687f70","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:37.001Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"44245dc2-5b5d-4fed-a141-14271db36053","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ad931174-fe43-46f9-80c6-7efe42e3ffb8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015MD69QTGE1kJM1CQry2MfB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Dask delayed futures distributed optimization solver Gurobi Benders 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Efficiency — Dask.distributed 2025.10.0+2.g9d7befe documentation\",\"url\":\"https://distributed.dask.org/en/latest/efficiency.html\"},{\"title\":\"Futures - non-blocking distributed calculations — Dask Tutorial documentation\",\"url\":\"https://tutorial.dask.org/05_futures.html\"},{\"title\":\"What is the pros/cons of using Futures/Delayed? - Distributed - Dask Forum\",\"url\":\"https://dask.discourse.group/t/what-is-the-pros-cons-of-using-futures-delayed/1394\"},{\"title\":\"Futures — dask 0.16.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://dask-local.readthedocs.io/en/latest/futures.html\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Different scheduling for dask delayed and dask futures? - Distributed - Dask Forum\",\"url\":\"https://dask.discourse.group/t/different-scheduling-for-dask-delayed-and-dask-futures/545\"},{\"title\":\"Futures — Dask 2.23.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://devdoc.net/python/dask-2.23.0-doc/futures.html\"},{\"title\":\"Managing Computation — Dask.distributed 2025.12.0.post7+gf4cfecc48 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://distributed.dask.org/en/latest/manage-computation.html\"},{\"title\":\"Decison Tree for Optimization Software\",\"url\":\"https://plato.asu.edu/bench.html\"},{\"title\":\"distributed and/or asynchronous algorithms for numeric methods · Issue #3241 · dask/dask\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dask/dask/issues/3241\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query on Dask delayed futures, distributed optimization solvers, Gurobi, and Benders decomposition. Here's what I found:\n\nThe search results contain general information about Dask's futures and delayed computation frameworks, along with some references to Gurobi optimization software, but they don't contain specific information combining all these topics together—particularly regarding Benders decomposition implementations with Dask and Gurobi in 2024-2025.\n\nThe results show:\n\n- Dask supports a real-time task framework that extends Python's concurrent.futures interface for arbitrary task scheduling, with features depending on the second generation task scheduler found in dask.distributed.\n\n- Unlike Dask collections like dask.delayed, task submissions with futures happen immediately, and the concurrent.futures interface is very similar to dask.delayed except that execution is immediate rather than lazy.\n\n- The Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual covers version 13.0, including Gurobi's modeling structures, features, and API concepts for developing applications.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific technical details about Benders decomposition implementation with Dask and Gurobi or recent developments in this area for 2024-2025. You may want to search for more specific resources like academic papers, Gurobi documentation on Benders decomposition, or Dask-specific optimization libraries if you need more targeted information on this topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8a2cfdc7-be83-4db9-9e18-a1d690961a9c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:37.599Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad931174-fe43-46f9-80c6-7efe42e3ffb8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c4a7089e-27db-48bc-a977-f96de4aee4a5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TpQ7YuV8HD4eYiRBkk7M7c","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ray distributed framework OR-Tools CP-SAT solver parallel 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"[1712.05889] Ray: A Distributed Framework for Emerging AI Applications\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.05889\"},{\"title\":\"On Continuous Optimization for Constraint Satisfaction Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.04480v1\"},{\"title\":\"Scale Machine Learning & AI Computing | Ray by Anyscale\",\"url\":\"https://www.ray.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Ray Clusters for AI: Distributed Computing Architecture | Introl Blog\",\"url\":\"https://introl.com/blog/ray-clusters-distributed-ai-computing-infrastructure-guide-2025\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"RAY: Distributed Computing Framework - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/machine-learning/ray-distributed-computing-framework/\"},{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about Ray distributed framework, OR-Tools CP-SAT solver, and parallel computing in 2025. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Key Results\n\n**OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver Performance:**\nGoogle's CP-SAT solver, part of OR-Tools, won gold medals at the Minizinc constraint programming competitions in editions 2018 up until 2025. OR-Tools CP-SAT is a hybrid solver that integrates a clause-learning SAT core, constraint programming, and linear relaxation within a unified model to solve combinatorial problems, and has effectively addressed many limitations of traditional CP solvers.\n\n**Ray Distributed Framework:**\nRay implements a unified interface that can express both task-parallel and actor-based computations, supported by a single dynamic execution engine. In 2025, OpenAI is using Ray to coordinate ChatGPT training, and Ray joined the PyTorch Foundation validating enterprise adoption.\n\n**Parallel Computing Capabilities:**\nRay supports fine-grained and coarse-grained parallelism, enabling many concurrent tasks and can efficiently distribute tasks across cores and machines in a cluster. For constraint solving, the rationale behind portfolio approaches lies in the inherent challenge of predicting which algorithm is best suited, so the pragmatic strategy involves running various approaches in parallel.\n\nThe search results show these are distinct but complementary technologies—Ray provides the distributed computing infrastructure, while CP-SAT provides the constraint solving engine, and they can be used together for scaling combinatorial optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"268118ff-ab0c-427b-a2fd-45a0f0125ff4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:37.661Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c4a7089e-27db-48bc-a977-f96de4aee4a5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"efe71546-40da-49c2-a49e-0a9e0fbe3e2e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LfuZZUh36c21oaifj58zpn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"distributed Benders decomposition Ray Python column generation 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition and column-and-row generation for solving large-scale linear programs with column-dependent-rows\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v264y2018i1p29-45.html\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benders_decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"benders-decomposition · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/benders-decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders Decomposition and Column Generation for Optimal Box Selection – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2025/12/combinatorial-benders-decomposition-and-column-generation-for-optimal-box-selection/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Benders Decomposition and Column-and-Row Generation for Solving Large-Scale Linear Programs with Column-Dependent-Rows\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/317785440_Benders_Decomposition_and_Column-and-Row_Generation_for_Solving_Large-Scale_Linear_Programs_with_Column-Dependent-Rows\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition and column-and-row generation for solving large-scale linear programs with column-dependent-rows - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221717305854\"},{\"title\":\"A column generation and Combinatorial Benders Decomposition algorithm for the Selective Dial-A-Ride-Problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054821003531\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - JuMP-dev\",\"url\":\"https://jump.dev/JuMP.jl/stable/tutorials/algorithms/benders_decomposition/\"},{\"title\":\"Combining Benders’ Decomposition and Column Generation for Integrated Crew Pairing and Personalized Crew Assignment Problems | Transportation Science\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/trsc.2019.0892\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing with Column Generation\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Book_on_Column_Generation___Part_I.pdf\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for \"distributed Benders decomposition Ray Python column generation 2024\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview of Results\n\nThe search returned relevant research and implementation resources on Benders decomposition and column generation, though specific results focusing on Ray framework integration appear limited in the results:\n\n**Academic Literature:**\nA novel integration of Benders cut generation and the simultaneous generation of columns and constraints yields a brand-new algorithm for solving large-scale CDR-problems. To solve two-stage problems, a cutting plane approach using Benders decomposition can be applied, where the master problem corresponds to the first stage, and Benders cuts can be generated by a purely combinatorial algorithm.\n\n**Algorithm Combinations:**\nMethods combining Benders' decomposition and column generation have been developed for complex optimization problems. An a priori column generation method combined with Combinatorial Benders Decomposition has been applied to vehicle routing problems.\n\n**Implementation Resources:**\nThe search identified several GitHub repositories and implementations of Benders decomposition in Python using Gurobi solvers, though specific 2024 implementations with Ray framework integration were not prominently featured in these results.\n\nThe results suggest that while Benders decomposition combined with column generation is an active research area, your specific query combining these techniques with Ray (a distributed computing framework) may require more targeted research into recent distributed optimization implementations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"59eb9153-3c2d-46dc-be61-f02300184238","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:39.002Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"efe71546-40da-49c2-a49e-0a9e0fbe3e2e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c060cb3f-d873-4241-acb0-a4d6efc736bc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E97mX7pvoqgR3ZaR9B5kLs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Ray\" \"spot instances\" cost optimization batch jobs cloud 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding Spot Instances Across AWS, Google Cloud, and Azure - ProsperOps\",\"url\":\"https://www.prosperops.com/blog/spot-instances/\"},{\"title\":\"Running Cost Effective Batch Workloads with AWS Batch and Amazon EC2 Spot Instances | AWS Online Tech Talks\",\"url\":\"https://pages.awscloud.com/Running-Cost-Effective-Batch-Workloads-with-AWS-Batch-and-Amazon-EC2-Spot-Instances_1022-CMP_OD.html\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon EC2 Spot Instances Guide 2026: Savings & Automatio | Sedai\",\"url\":\"https://sedai.io/blog/optimizing-spot-instances-in-aws\"},{\"title\":\"Spot Instances: How to Reduce Cloud Costs by 90% - Cast AI\",\"url\":\"https://cast.ai/blog/reduce-cloud-costs-with-spot-instances/\"},{\"title\":\"Spot Instances and Preemptible GPUs: Cutting AI Costs by 70% | Introl Blog\",\"url\":\"https://introl.com/blog/spot-instances-preemptible-gpus-ai-cost-savings\"},{\"title\":\"Spot instances vs. on-demand instances: Pros and cons\",\"url\":\"https://www.flexera.com/blog/finops/spot-instances-vs-on-demand-instances-pros-and-cons/\"},{\"title\":\"What are AWS Spot Instances? Guide to lower cloud costs and avoid downtime | Blog — Northflank\",\"url\":\"https://northflank.com/blog/spot-instances\"},{\"title\":\"What Are Spot Instances? Strategies to Reduce Cloud Costs\",\"url\":\"https://www.tierpoint.com/blog/cloud/spot-instances/\"},{\"title\":\"SkyServe: Serving AI Models across Regions and Clouds with Spot Instances\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2411.01438v2\"},{\"title\":\"How to Save Cost on EC2 with AWS Spot Instance Advisor\",\"url\":\"https://www.economize.cloud/blog/aws-spot-instance-advisor/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Ray, spot instances, cost optimization for batch jobs in cloud environments:\n\n## Ray and Spot Instance Integration\n\nRay Tune automatically handles spot instance failures, restarting terminated jobs on new instances, with organizations reporting 75% cost savings for hyperparameter searches using spot instances exclusively.\n\n## Spot Instances for Batch Jobs\n\nSpot Instances are recommended for bursty, fault-tolerant tasks like batch processing or containerized jobs. Spot Instances are well-suited for running interruptible batch processing tasks, such as financial modeling, scientific simulations, or media encoding.\n\n## Cost Savings\n\nThe potential savings are significant: Spot Instances can cut compute spend by as much as 90 percent compared to On-Demand pricing. Recent Kubernetes benchmarks show that clusters with a mix of On-Demand and Spot Instances recorded an average savings of 59%, while clusters running only Spot Instances scored a 77% reduction on average.\n\n## Key Considerations for 2025\n\nAs of December 2025, spot and on-demand GPU prices have converged significantly as supply constraints eased, with AWS cutting on-demand H100 prices 44% in June 2025, narrowing the spot premium advantage. This suggests that while spot instances remain valuable for batch jobs, the cost differential has decreased compared to previous years.\n\n## Best Practices\n\nTo run workloads reliably on Spot Instances, use an automation solution that manages the entire Spot lifecycle, from provisioning and managing interruptions to moving workloads to On-Demand in case of a Spot drought.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3493315a-837d-4071-a5a0-97fac080591e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:41.344Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c060cb3f-d873-4241-acb0-a4d6efc736bc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"927da3ff-f74e-47c9-aa89-b06545043a4f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpGjmqT71sGLZTSMUzooUn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ray RLlib reinforcement learning branching SAT solver MIP 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Scale Machine Learning & AI Computing | Ray by Anyscale\",\"url\":\"https://www.ray.io/\"},{\"title\":\"RLlib: Industry-Grade, Scalable Reinforcement Learning — Ray 2.55.1\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/rllib/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"arXiv:2403.19446v2 [cs.LO] 2 Jul 2025 Logic Optimization Meets SAT: A Novel\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.19446\"},{\"title\":\"[2505.16053] Learning from Algorithm Feedback: One-Shot SAT Solver Guidance with GNNs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16053\"},{\"title\":\"Ray RLlib ML Library for Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.anyscale.com/product/library/ray-rllib\"},{\"title\":\"Improving SAT Solver Heuristics with Graph Networks and Reinforcement Learning | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=B1lCn64tvS\"},{\"title\":\"4. Reinforcement Learning with Ray RLlib - Learning Ray [Book]\",\"url\":\"https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/learning-ray/9781098117214/ch04.html\"},{\"title\":\"RLlib: Industry-Grade, Scalable Reinforcement Learning — Ray 2.52.1\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/rllib/\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started — Ray 2.55.1 - Ray Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/rllib/getting-started.html\"},{\"title\":\"RLlib: Abstractions for Distributed Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1712.09381\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding your query about Ray RLlib, reinforcement learning, branching SAT solver, and MIP in 2025:\n\n## Ray RLlib Overview\n\nRLlib is an open source library for reinforcement learning (RL), offering support for production-level, highly scalable, and fault-tolerant RL workloads, while maintaining simple and unified APIs for a large variety of industry applications.\n\n## Reinforcement Learning for SAT Solver Branching\n\nThere are several recent research efforts combining reinforcement learning with SAT solver branching heuristics:\n\n1. **RLAF Approach (May 2025)**: Reinforcement Learning from Algorithm Feedback (RLAF) is a paradigm for learning to guide SAT solver branching heuristics with Graph Neural Networks (GNNs). RLAF-trained policies significantly reduce the mean solve times of different base solvers across diverse SAT problem distributions, achieving more than a 2x speedup in some cases.\n\n2. **Logic Synthesis with RL (July 2025)**: An RL-guided logic synthesis pipeline for optimizing circuit transformations and a cost-customized LUT mapping strategy minimizes branching complexity during SAT solving. Experiments demonstrate significant runtime reductions—up to 63% compared to baseline approaches.\n\n3. **GQSAT (Earlier Research)**: GQSAT is a branching heuristic in a Boolean SAT solver trained with value-based reinforcement learning (RL) using Graph Neural Networks for function approximation.\n\nHowever, the search results do not show specific applications that directly combine Ray RLlib with SAT solvers or MIP solvers. The results show that RLlib is a general-purpose RL platform, while the SAT solver research uses other RL approaches.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6f7c654a-b439-496f-b5ac-7c35be7d9a78","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:41.673Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"927da3ff-f74e-47c9-aa89-b06545043a4f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
