{"parentUuid":"f5e015b2-27b1-4f4e-8948-174cf067e09c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014AoRnvdZJh5hQn35cH9owz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ray Job Submission long running campaign solver checkpoint resume 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Ray Jobs Overview — Ray 2.55.1 - Ray Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/cluster/running-applications/job-submission/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Ray Job Dispatch and Tuning — Isaac Lab Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://isaac-sim.github.io/IsaacLab/main/source/features/ray.html\"},{\"title\":\"[jobs] Submit, Stop, and Delete Job Hanging on a Ray Cluster After a Period of Time · Issue #38605 · ray-project/ray\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ray-project/ray/issues/38605\"},{\"title\":\"RayJob Quickstart — Ray 2.55.1\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/cluster/kubernetes/getting-started/rayjob-quick-start.html\"},{\"title\":\"What is the proper way to submit a job to the cluster? · Issue #5356 · ray-project/ray\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ray-project/ray/issues/5356\"},{\"title\":\"ray/doc/source/cluster/running-applications/job-submission/index.md at master · ray-project/ray\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ray-project/ray/blob/master/doc/source/cluster/running-applications/job-submission/index.md\"},{\"title\":\"[dashboard] [RFC] Job submission · Issue #13395 · ray-project/ray\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ray-project/ray/issues/13395\"},{\"title\":\"ray.job_submission.JobSubmissionClient.submit_job — Ray 2.54.0\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/cluster/running-applications/job-submission/doc/ray.job_submission.JobSubmissionClient.submit_job.html\"},{\"title\":\"ray.job_submission.JobStatus — Ray 2.37.0 - Ray Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/cluster/running-applications/job-submission/doc/ray.job_submission.JobStatus.html\"},{\"title\":\"Submit a job in a Ray cluster - Container Service for ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/ack/cloud-native-ai-suite/use-cases/submit-a-ray-job\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for \"Ray Job Submission long running campaign solver checkpoint resume 2025\". \n\nThe search results provide general information about Ray job submission, including:\n\n- Ray Jobs API quickstart guides and APIs for programmatic job submission and REST-based submission\n- RayJob submission modes including K8sJobMode, HTTPMode, InteractiveMode, and SidecarMode\n- Information about submitting Ray jobs using the `ray job submit` command\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about \"long running campaign solver,\" checkpoint resume functionality, or 2025-specific features related to these terms. The results primarily cover general Ray job submission APIs and Kubernetes deployment of Ray jobs.\n\nIf you're looking for more specific information about campaign solver checkpointing or resuming long-running jobs with specific 2025 features, could you provide more context about what you're trying to accomplish? This would help me perform a more targeted search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f9b2d44c-6c1a-4bdb-b5c7-65f306af387e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:52.757Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5e015b2-27b1-4f4e-8948-174cf067e09c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"377258b1-2a69-484e-a55b-303336c7fc29","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0148raPs8pakNysBegausaL1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cpsat-autotune CP-SAT parameters Ray Tune integration ALNS 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-autotune: WIP: Tune the hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver for specific models · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-autotune · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-autotune/0.2.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-autotune\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-autotune/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT model on C++\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/u8yiW5KXioU\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Discover OR-Tools CP-SAT, Google's constraint solver | COSLING\",\"url\":\"https://www.cosling.com/cpsat\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cpsat-autotune and its integration with CP-SAT parameters and ALNS:\n\n## Overview\n\ncpsat-autotune provides a method for tuning the CP-SAT solver's hyperparameters to minimize the time required to find an optimal solution, which is useful when you need a guaranteed solution without a fixed time limit.\n\n## ALNS Integration\n\ncpsat-autotune is specifically designed to enhance solver efficiency in targeted scenarios, particularly within the context of Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS), where the CP-SAT solver is frequently invoked with a strict time limit to solve similar problem instances as part of a larger iterative optimization process.\n\nInstead of completely replacing the CP-SAT solver with a single tuned configuration, cpsat-autotune allows you to tune hyperparameters for one or more specific instance sets and incorporate these as additional strategies within ALNS, maintaining the default CP-SAT parameters while augmenting the solver's capability with tailored configurations, and allowing ALNS to automatically select the most effective strategy for each iteration.\n\n## CLI Commands\n\nThe cpsat-autotune CLI provides two main commands: time and quality, with the time command tuning CP-SAT hyperparameters to minimize the time required to find an optimal solution.\n\nThe search results focus on cpsat-autotune's functionality and documentation, though they don't contain specific information about Ray Tune integration or 2025-specific updates. The project is available on GitHub and PyPI as an open-source tool for CP-SAT hyperparameter optimization.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b057f93a-9e5c-4dea-919f-d9a8bd0038da","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:52.765Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"377258b1-2a69-484e-a55b-303336c7fc29","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"675b62ea-4bab-4a75-b3e0-d5c3edd42a5d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018P6GrVaFdMUte6v8bomm8d","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ray vs Dask vs multiprocessing benchmark 2025 task parallelism overhead\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Analyzing Memory Management & Performance in Dask-on-Ray\",\"url\":\"https://www.anyscale.com/blog/analyzing-memory-management-and-performance-in-dask-on-ray\"},{\"title\":\"Spark, Dask, and Ray: Choosing the Right Framework\",\"url\":\"https://domino.ai/blog/spark-dask-ray-choosing-the-right-framework\"},{\"title\":\"Ray vs Dask vs Apache Spark™ — Comparing Data Science & Machine Learning Engines\",\"url\":\"https://www.onehouse.ai/blog/apache-spark-vs-ray-vs-dask-comparing-data-science-machine-learning-engines\"},{\"title\":\"Ray or Dask? A Practical Guide for Data Scientists - KDnuggets\",\"url\":\"https://www.kdnuggets.com/ray-or-dask-a-practical-guide-for-data-scientists\"},{\"title\":\"Ray vs Dask: Lessons learned serving 240k models per day in real-time | by Emergent Methods | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://emergentmethods.medium.com/ray-vs-dask-lessons-learned-serving-240k-models-per-day-in-real-time-7863c8968a1f\"},{\"title\":\"PySpark, Dask or Ray, how to scale your python workloads?\",\"url\":\"https://dataroots.io/blog/pyspark-dask-or-ray\"},{\"title\":\"Flexible parallel processing using the R future and Python Dask packages\",\"url\":\"https://computing.stat.berkeley.edu/tutorial-dask-future/\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison to dask · Issue #642 ray-project/ray · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ray-project/ray/issues/642\"},{\"title\":\"Shared Memory — Dask documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.dask.org/en/latest/shared.html\"},{\"title\":\"PySpark vs Dask vs Polars vs Ray Explained: When to Use What | by Shubham Saxena | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@shubhamsd100/pyspark-vs-dask-vs-polars-vs-ray-explained-when-to-use-what-5a1308828aa9\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Ray vs Dask vs multiprocessing benchmark comparisons:\n\n## Performance Comparison\n\nRay works around 10% faster than Python standard multiprocessing, even on a single node. This suggests Ray has lower overhead compared to the standard multiprocessing library.\n\n## Scaling and Architecture Differences\n\nThe general agreement as of 2023 is that Ray can scale far beyond Dask due to its decentralized scheduling scheme, but Dask is more user-friendly and more performant for out-of-memory data manipulations.\n\n## Task Parallelism Overhead\n\nRegarding overhead in general, distributed data processing frameworks come with overhead, and this is introduced computationally by the need to manage the distribution of the workloads and deal with fault tolerance.\n\nFor memory handling specifically, Dask with multithreading and Dask-on-Ray can both take advantage of memory sharing to avoid copies, but Dask with multiprocessing requires copying the object.\n\n## Current Status (2025)\n\nThe search results show some recent 2025 comparisons, though they don't contain specific 2025 benchmark data comparing task parallelism overhead across all three frameworks. The most recent comprehensive comparison suggests that the choice depends heavily on your workload: Ray excels at machine learning workloads, Dask is better for data-processing tasks, and multiprocessing remains the baseline for simple cases but with higher overhead than Ray.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"136f878a-eb3f-4ec4-a1b1-bc1e59377167","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:53.107Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"675b62ea-4bab-4a75-b3e0-d5c3edd42a5d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"779063ff-63ef-4245-b6d1-73e1aa20b6cd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GdNu1MEW5PWgnoAzycmSQd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"D-Painless distributed portfolio SAT solving 2024 2025 framework\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/391418351_D-Painless_A_Framework_for_Distributed_Portfolio_SAT_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving - Archive ouverte HAL\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-05084417\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving in the Serverless Cloud - Stanford CS Theory\",\"url\":\"http://theory.stanford.edu/~barrett/pubs/OWB21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"HordeSat: A Massively Parallel Portfolio SAT Solver | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/276296424_HordeSat_A_Massively_Parallel_Portfolio_SAT_Solver\"},{\"title\":\"HordeSat: A Massively Parallel Portfolio SAT Solver | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-24318-4_12\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: A Framework for Parallel SAT Solving | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318986849_PaInleSS_A_Framework_for_Parallel_SAT_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - lip6/painless: A framework to ease parallelization of sequential SAT solvers\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lip6/painless\"},{\"title\":\"Modular and Efficient Divide-and-Conquer SAT Solver on Top of the Painless Framework - Archive ouverte HAL\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-02093520\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] PaInleSS: A Framework for Parallel SAT Solving | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/PaInleSS:-A-Framework-for-Parallel-SAT-Solving-Frioux-Baarir/8d6870ab6c3abbb7b952fde8ffb2e57da8bf2747\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about D-Painless and the distributed portfolio SAT solving framework:\n\n## D-Painless: Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving\n\nD-Painless is a new extension of the Painless framework to include the distributed portfolio strategy and clause sharing, aiming to broaden Painless's functionality for more effective and comprehensive distributed SAT solving methodologies.\n\n### Key Context and Approach\n\nThe portfolio strategy, combined with clause sharing, has emerged as the leading approach for both local and distributed parallelization on CPUs. Frameworks such as Mallob exemplify the effectiveness of this strategy by providing a straightforward method to deploy portfolio parallel solvers across various computing environments.\n\n### Framework Capabilities\n\nThe Painless framework specializes in local parallelization, offering diverse strategies for task sharing and parallel execution, enabling the adoption of complex hybrid local parallelization techniques, including portfolio, divide-and-conquer, and cube-and-conquer methods.\n\n### Publication Details\n\nThe paper \"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving\" was authored by Saoudi, M., Baarir, S., Sopena, J., Lejemble, T., and published in Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems (TACAS 2025).\n\n### Technical Infrastructure\n\nWhile developing a portfolio distributed SAT solver is complex due to communication synchronization, data bufferization, and multiple threads, the framework's architecture hides this complexity by clearly separating the different needed behaviors in well-defined interfaces, guiding the developer in using network communication only where needed.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1d268640-61be-4077-ac24-8a0d83defd3e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:01:54.729Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"779063ff-63ef-4245-b6d1-73e1aa20b6cd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1d268640-61be-4077-ac24-8a0d83defd3e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acbb24f80720aa3e3","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WEZZxXyL3p5CmnzDVx58gi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough data to draft the synthesis. No need for more searches.\n\n# Ray / Dask / 分布式框架在 SAT/CP 求解扩展的应用调研（2024-2026）\n\n## 1. 主要框架对比\n\n| 维度 | multiprocessing（现状） | Ray 2.55+ | Dask Distributed | Spark/Mallob/D-Painless |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 单机调度开销 | 高（fork+pickle） | ~比 mp 快 10%；任务粒度 ≥1ms 即可 | 多线程零拷贝；多进程需 pickle | Spark JVM 重；Mallob 是 MPI 原生 |\n| 跨机扩展 | 无 | 原生（gRPC + GCS） | 原生（TCP scheduler） | MPI（Mallob/D-Painless）/ YARN |\n| Spot/抢占容错 | 无 | 内置（Ray Tune 自动迁移，案例报告 75% 成本节省） | `Client.retire_workers` 手动 | 较弱 |\n| 长跑作业 | 无 | Ray Jobs API（REST 提交，状态机 PENDING/RUNNING/SUCCEEDED/FAILED） | 通过 `Future` + scheduler 暴露 | Spark Driver 长跑 |\n| OR/SAT 应用案例 | 通用 | OpenAI ChatGPT 训练协调；Ray Tune 集成 Optuna 调 CP-SAT 参数 | 数值计算偏多，OR 案例少 | TACAS 2025: D-Painless（lip6/painless 之上扩 MPI） |\n\n关键 API 速查：\n- Ray：`@ray.remote`（task）、`ray.put/get`（对象 store，零拷贝 NumPy）、`ray.tune.Tuner` + `optuna.OptunaSearch`、`JobSubmissionClient.submit_job(entrypoint=..., runtime_env=...)`\n- Dask：`dask.delayed(fn)(...)`、`Client.submit/gather`、`client.scatter` 广播只读对象\n- cpsat-autotune：CLI `time/quality/gap`，三个 trial 参数（`n_samples_for_trial`、`n_samples_for_verification`、`n_trials`），底层用 Optuna；可直接接 Ray Tune 当作搜索 backend\n\n## 2. 跟我们项目的 PoC 路径\n\n外层并行点很自然契合 Ray：\n1. **第一步（最小成本）**：把 `src/search/exact_parallel_scheduler.py` 的 multiprocessing.Pool 换成 Ray 的 `@ray.remote` task，保持单机 4 worker 不变。每候选 ≈ 6h 远超调度开销，吞吐没损失。`ray.put` 把 `candidate_placements.json` / `mandatory_exact_instances.json`（只读、几 MB）放进对象 store，避免每个 worker 重 pickle。工程量预估：300-500 行改动 + 1 天调试。\n2. **第二步（多机 spot）**：用 Ray on Kubernetes（KubeRay）或 Anyscale 起 spot 集群，每 spot 节点跑一个 candidate，用 `max_task_retries` 自动迁移被回收的实例。Campaign 状态写 S3/OSS，断点恢复用现有 `exact_campaign.py` 检查点机制。CP-SAT 本身是 CPU bound，spot 中断后从最近 checkpoint 重跑该候选——**不能恢复 CP-SAT 内部搜索状态**，只能丢弃当前候选的部分进度。\n3. **第三步（C lane 集成）**：Ray Tune + Optuna 跑 CP-SAT 参数 sweep（S6 stage matrix 的下一代），把 cpsat-autotune 的逻辑接进来。这跟 AI Safety Contract 兼容（仅 hint，不是 proof source）。\n4. **慎做**：RLlib for branching。SAT 圈的 RL（GQSAT、RLAF 2025，2x 加速）是改 SAT 求解器内部的，CP-SAT 是闭源 C++，无 hook 点；除非自研 SAT 内核否则不沾。\n\n## 3. 云成本估算（100 候选 × 6h）\n\n总 600 CPU-hour。AWS c7i.2xlarge（8 vCPU）on-demand ≈ \\$0.36/h，spot ≈ \\$0.10-0.14/h（2025 年差距收窄，AWS 6 月降价 44% 后差不多 60-70% off）。\n- On-demand：100 候选 × 6h ÷ 8 vCPU/节点 × $0.36 ≈ **\\$27**（极便宜，因 CP-SAT 单线程为主）\n- Spot 100% 跑：≈ **\\$8-10**\n- Ray cluster overhead（head node t3.medium 24/7）：~\\$0.5/天\n\n**结论**：钱不是瓶颈，瓶颈是工程时间和 spot 中断的恢复语义。\n\n## 4. Ray Jobs 作为 campaign runtime\n\n`ray job submit --runtime-env-json='{\"working_dir\": \"...\", \"pip\": [...]}' -- python main.py --campaign-hours 168` 可以替代当前的本地 Python 进程。优势：dashboard 可视化、日志聚合、远程提交；劣势：增加一层进程管理抽象，本地开发要装 ray + 起 head 节点。168h campaign 完全 fit Ray Jobs（已知 issue #38605 是 idle 长跑悬挂，活跃 job 不受影响）。\n\n## 5. 是否值得引入 Ray\n\n**当前阶段（Phase 3B 单机优化）：不值得**。理由：\n- 4 worker 单机用 multiprocessing 已经够用，Ray 在单机只快 ~10%，换框架的工程量（500 行 + 测试套件适配）不划算\n- AI Safety Contract 限制 Ray Tune/RLlib 不能动 proof path，可加入但属于 nice-to-have\n- Spot 中断对 CP-SAT 这种长跑单线程任务的\"中途丢弃\"特别痛，需要重设计 checkpoint 粒度（细化到候选级即可，不需 Ray）\n\n**值得引入的明确触发条件**：\n1. Phase 3C 要扩到 ≥3 个 base（valley4_infra_outpost 等），候选数 ×3-5 倍，单机周转超 1 周——这时 Ray on KubeRay + spot 节省不止时间，而是日历周期\n2. C lane 真要做 CP-SAT 参数 sweep 大于 100 个 trial，Ray Tune + Optuna 是直接收益（仍是 sidecar，shadow-only，不破坏 lock）\n3. 落地时机推荐 Phase 3C 启动前做 Lane B 扩展，**先在 sweep 上试 Ray Tune（低风险、AI sidecar 兼容），不动 outer search 主路径**\n\n简言之：现在不上，Phase 3C 多 base 扩张时上，先从 Tune sidecar 切入，主求解路径保留 multiprocessing 直到必须分布式。\n\n## Sources\n- [Ray docs](https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/)\n- [Ray Tune index](https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/tune/index.html)\n- [Ray Jobs Overview](https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/cluster/running-applications/job-submission/index.html)\n- [cpsat-autotune GitHub](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune)\n- [CP-SAT Primer (parameters)](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [D-Painless: Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving (TACAS 2025)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3)\n- [RLAF: Learning from Algorithm Feedback (arXiv 2505.16053)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16053)\n- [Ray vs Dask 实战对比（Emergent Methods）](https://emergentmethods.medium.com/ray-vs-dask-lessons-learned-serving-240k-models-per-day-in-real-time-7863c8968a1f)\n- [Spark/Dask/Ray 对比（Domino）](https://domino.ai/blog/spark-dask-ray-choosing-the-right-framework)\n- [Ray clusters 架构 2025（Introl）](https://introl.com/blog/ray-clusters-distributed-ai-computing-infrastructure-guide-2025)\n- [AWS Spot 价格趋势 2025（Introl）](https://introl.com/blog/spot-instances-preemptible-gpus-ai-cost-savings)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1189,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5819,"cache_read_input_tokens":27534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5819,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxnRdBzv1goDUcTKW2U","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c59feec4-929b-4c43-879a-0adfa77a3c0d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:53.878Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
